2026-09-26 — K11g, delayed dying-memcg release; classification closed below.

FINAL-REFERENCE FOLLOW-UP (same day):
Add css_release stack triggers and local page/object drain probes. Both trace
capture assertions PASS, no lost events, both boot/shutdown predicates PASS.
After 20s idle, reference retains 5 offlined memcg identities; subject retains 8.
Every identity (5/5 and 8/8) has a matched final css_release(ref=css+16) and
mem_cgroup_css_released(css). Each final-reference stack contains
folio_batch_move_lru -> folios_put_refs -> __mem_cgroup_uncharge_folios ->
uncharge_folio/uncharge_batch -> css_release. Reference releases four on root
activity and the fifth on later faults; subject releases all eight on root
activity. The per-CPU folio batch owns the references, not a demonstrated empty
charge-stock slot. Source mm/swap.c takes folio_get in __folio_batch_add_and_move
and releases via folios_put in folio_batch_move_lru; this is a matching measured
kernel path on both compilers, not merely the observation that both fail.

Identity analysis snapshots offlined-minus-released at the idle marker; later
address reuse must not overwrite that set. All delayed identities have witnesses.
The initial analysis incorrectly retained only the final offline per address;
its 2-vs-5 assertion failed. Correct chronological handling gives 5/5 and 8/8.

Unchanged cgroup:test_kmem, existing matched full runtimes, same 45s limit:
reference inner 4 PASS / 2 FAIL; subject inner 3 PASS / 3 FAIL. Both outer FAIL,
both boot/shutdown PASS. Dead-group test still FAILs (3/2 dying at its last wait);
missing-slab test still FAILs. Subject also fails deletion accounting:
memory.current 5890048, sum 4841472, difference 1048576 == MAX_VMSTAT_ERROR,
where the original requires strictly less. This is separate from K11g; its
subsequent seven-slot capacity classification is in cgroup-stock-capacity.out.
No original assertion/flag/budget changed; no kernel patch or compiler workaround.
K11g closes classification only, not original-test PASS or fresh full acceptance.

