EARLIER OBSERVATION AND HYPOTHESIS (superseded by attribution above):

Reuse frozen test_kmem.c functions, not a rewritten stress workload:
30 groups through cg_run_in_subcgroups(parent, alloc_dcache, (void*)100, 30),
and 100 groups through alloc_kmem_smp. Preserve the helper's ignored argument.
Observe for 20s, then perform 8 root-cgroup fork/affinity/one-page cycles on
each of 4 CPUs; observe 3s; only then charge 8 distinct memcgs per CPU and
observe 5s. All control memcgs are outside the measured parent and stay alive
until observation completes. This diagnostic does not alter original limits.

Retained original-group dying counts after idle / root-control / displacement:
GCC: 5 / 0 / 0. EvoCC: 4 / 0 / 0.
Threaded-group counts: GCC 2 / 0 / 0; EvoCC 8 / 0 / 0.
All four exit zero as observation completion; no TAP was emitted, so the generic
selftest parser correctly records INVALID_OUTPUT, not PASS. Both boot/shutdown
predicates PASS. Do not infer an original test PASS from these observations.

Follow-up trace wrapper reuses the exact stock ELF and original-group path.
Frozen BTF layout: stock nr_pages[7] offset 1, cached[7] offset 8, css offset 0.
Kprobes record stock draining, memcg offlining/release and observation markers.
GCC: idle retains 3, then all three releases at 21.225685..21.225742 seconds.
EvoCC: idle retains 5, then releases at 25.559410..25.590174 seconds.
Both reach zero before the distinct-stock phase. No out-of-line drain_stock
event occurs during that release interval, but inlined paths are not ruled out.
All per-CPU overrun/commit-overrun/dropped counters are zero. Two trace-capture
assertions PASS and both boot/shutdown predicates PASS. Capture completion
does not establish the exact reference owner or waive original failure.

The upstream report "mm: memcg: release the css reference when a stock slot
empties" describes a real matching source pattern, not demonstrated causality:
https://lkml.rescloud.iu.edu/2608.2/04093.html
Root activity clearing the population before displacement is a critical control.
Next: capture the final css_release caller, including inlined drain paths.
